And there's this guy that I know
and he's very into like Bitcoin

481
00:24:47,317 --> 00:24:49,584
and cryptocurrencies
and stuff like that.

482
00:24:49,686 --> 00:24:54,389
He posted this article and it
says, "Ross Ulbricht Arrested."

483
00:24:54,491 --> 00:24:57,359
And I pull up Lyn's, uh,
g-chat and I'm like,

484
00:24:57,461 --> 00:24:59,928
"What is going on?
Like why is..."

485
00:25:00,030 --> 00:25:01,563
And I'm looking at Ross' page...

486
00:25:01,665 --> 00:25:03,732
Picture, you know,
about being arrested.

487
00:25:03,834 --> 00:25:05,300
What is this?

488
00:25:05,402 --> 00:25:07,068
She says, "We don't even know.

489
00:25:07,170 --> 00:25:08,770
We're leaving Costa Rica
right now."

490
00:25:08,872 --> 00:25:11,973
I mean, they were on their way,
but it blew my mind.

491
00:25:12,075 --> 00:25:13,975
I mean totally blew my mind.

492
00:25:18,148 --> 00:25:20,315
- REEVES NARRATING:
Ross William Ulbricht grew up

493
00:25:20,417 --> 00:25:24,119
in a suburb of Austin,
the only son of Kirk and Lyn

494
00:25:24,221 --> 00:25:26,421
with an older sister
named Callie.

495
00:25:26,523 --> 00:25:29,557
It's a loving, tight-knit,
middle-class family.

496
00:25:29,659 --> 00:25:32,427
The Ulbrichts earn their income
from properties they built

497
00:25:32,529 --> 00:25:35,630
and rent on
the Costa Rican coast.

498
00:25:35,732 --> 00:25:39,634
Ross was an avid outdoorsman,
an Eagle Scout like his father,

499
00:25:39,736 --> 00:25:43,004
and displayed
an early aptitude for math.

500
00:25:43,106 --> 00:25:44,406
Ross earned a full scholarship

501
00:25:44,508 --> 00:25:48,576
to the University of Texas
at Dallas studying Physics.

502
00:25:48,678 --> 00:25:53,014
He graduated in 2006 and then
won another full scholarship

503
00:25:53,116 --> 00:25:54,616
to Penn State
to pursue a Masters

504
00:25:54,718 --> 00:25:57,619
in Material Science
and Engineering.

505
00:25:57,721 --> 00:26:00,522
It was at Penn State that
Ross began a deep interest

506
00:26:00,624 --> 00:26:04,426
in Libertarianism, particularly
the work of Ludwig von Mises

507
00:26:04,528 --> 00:26:06,661
and the Austrian School
of Economics.

508
00:26:06,763 --> 00:26:09,864
Yet by 2009,
having completed his Masters,

509
00:26:09,966 --> 00:26:12,700
Ross seemed to be having
a change of life plan

510
00:26:12,803 --> 00:26:15,103
telling his mother
he no longer had an interest

511
00:26:15,205 --> 00:26:17,338
in pursuing a career in science

512
00:26:17,441 --> 00:26:20,375
and instead wanted to
become an entrepreneur.

513
00:26:20,477 --> 00:26:22,444
- REEVES NARRATING:
Ross moved back to Austin

514
00:26:22,546 --> 00:26:25,013
and opened his own used book
company, Good Wagon,

515
00:26:25,115 --> 00:26:27,715
donating a portion of
the proceeds to an inner city

516
00:26:27,818 --> 00:26:31,619
youth program and to
a prison literacy project.

517
00:26:31,721 --> 00:26:34,355
- I remember him saying,
when we had coffee,

518
00:26:34,458 --> 00:26:36,825
the last time we saw each other,
I remember him saying

519
00:26:36,927 --> 00:26:40,762
that he wished he had joined
a fraternity in college.

520
00:26:40,864 --> 00:26:42,797
And I remember saying,
"Well, that's surprising."

521
00:26:42,899 --> 00:26:45,567
You know, I didn't really
understand that perspective,

522
00:26:45,669 --> 00:26:50,071
um, and I just remember him
thinking, well he focused a lot

523
00:26:50,173 --> 00:26:55,510
on his studies in school and
maybe didn't create the social

524
00:26:55,612 --> 00:26:59,981
network that he was looking
for, um, in... in school.

525
00:27:00,083 --> 00:27:04,219
But as far as where we saw each
other going or where we saw

526
00:27:04,321 --> 00:27:10,492
ourselves going, um, I think
we both had a strong desire

527
00:27:10,594 --> 00:27:13,461
to be in control of our destiny.

528
00:27:13,563 --> 00:27:15,683
You know, again like when
he started the book company,

529
00:27:15,699 --> 00:27:17,432
uh, totally natural.

530
00:27:17,534 --> 00:27:19,467
Not even something that
I would have questioned,

531
00:27:19,569 --> 00:27:21,302
where there are a lot of people

532
00:27:21,404 --> 00:27:23,238
that would never start
their own business.

533
00:27:23,340 --> 00:27:24,973
But for Ross, sure,
you know, why not?

534
00:27:25,075 --> 00:27:26,708
- REEVES NARRATING:
But the business floundered

535
00:27:26,810 --> 00:27:28,977
and Ross eventually
shut it down.

536
00:27:29,079 --> 00:27:32,180
And if a post on his Linkedln
page was any indication,

537
00:27:32,282 --> 00:27:34,349
Ross had experienced
a kind of epiphany

538
00:27:34,451 --> 00:27:36,951
on the next way forward.

539
00:27:37,053 --> 00:27:39,854
Ulbricht wrote,
"Now my goals have shifted.

540
00:27:39,956 --> 00:27:42,790
"I want to use economic theory
as a means to abolish

541
00:27:42,893 --> 00:27:45,960
"the use of coercion and
aggression amongst mankind.

542
00:27:46,062 --> 00:27:49,898
"To that end, I am creating
an economic simulation to give

543
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:52,267
"people a first-hand experience
of what it would be like

544
00:27:52,369 --> 00:27:56,137
to live in a world without
the systemic use of force."

545
00:27:56,239 --> 00:27:58,273
From this moment, in late 2010,

546
00:27:58,375 --> 00:28:00,675
Ross became something
of a free spirit,

547
00:28:00,777 --> 00:28:03,077
eventually leaving
his parents' home in Austin

548
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:05,780
to live with his sister Callie
in Sydney, Australia

549
00:28:05,882 --> 00:28:08,216
and then returning
briefly to Austin.

550
00:28:08,318 --> 00:28:10,985
Throughout this period,
as far as his family knew,

551
00:28:11,087 --> 00:28:12,754
Ross' means of employment

552
00:28:12,856 --> 00:28:16,224
was working on freelance
projects in computer finance.

553
00:28:16,326 --> 00:28:19,360
- I am Rene Pinnell, age 29.

554
00:28:19,462 --> 00:28:21,896
Today is December 6, 2012

555
00:28:21,998 --> 00:28:25,900
and we are in the Jewish
Contemporary Art Museum,

556
00:28:26,002 --> 00:28:32,607
and relationship to partner
is best friend.

557
00:28:32,709 --> 00:28:35,677
So, Ross, how did you come
to live in San Francisco?

558
00:28:35,779 --> 00:28:39,714
- Uh, you twisted
my arm until I said,

559
00:28:39,816 --> 00:28:42,750
"Ah, fine I'll come."
[laughing]

560
00:28:42,852 --> 00:28:45,587
I get a phone call from Rene,
"Ross, call me up.

561
00:28:45,689 --> 00:28:47,922
I've got an opportunity
for you."

562
00:28:48,024 --> 00:28:49,657
I'm like, "Okay."

563
00:28:49,759 --> 00:28:51,659
He's like, "Yeah, I'm doing
a startup here in San Francisco.

564
00:28:51,761 --> 00:28:54,195
Um, I want you to
be a part of it."

565
00:28:54,297 --> 00:28:56,731
The more I thought about it,
and the more he, um,

566
00:28:56,833 --> 00:29:01,569
laid out the pros
and cons, uh... uh...

567
00:29:01,671 --> 00:29:03,371
the more it all just
seemed like cosmic

568
00:29:03,473 --> 00:29:07,875
and the right thing to do.
So, um, yeah.

569
00:29:07,978 --> 00:29:09,711
I bought my ticket
and two weeks later

570
00:29:09,813 --> 00:29:12,380
I showed up at his doorstep.

571
00:29:12,482 --> 00:29:14,048
- REEVES NARRATING: As Ross
Ulbricht was making his way

572
00:29:14,150 --> 00:29:17,952
from Australia to Austin,
and eventually to San Francisco,

573
00:29:18,054 --> 00:29:21,022
the Silk Road was online
and growing steadily.

574
00:29:21,124 --> 00:29:22,457
So naturally it sparked
the attention

575
00:29:22,559 --> 00:29:24,292
of federal law enforcement

576
00:29:24,394 --> 00:29:26,060
and specifically
the wing of the DHS

577
00:29:26,162 --> 00:29:28,930
called Homeland Security
Investigations,

578
00:29:29,032 --> 00:29:32,867
housed in the old Customs House
in Baltimore, Maryland.

579
00:29:32,969 --> 00:29:35,970
- You have postal
inspectors in Seattle

580
00:29:36,072 --> 00:29:37,639
and Customs and Border
Protection, uh,

581
00:29:37,741 --> 00:29:40,708
intercepting mail shipments
coming from overseas

582
00:29:40,810 --> 00:29:43,911
full of drugs, full of,
uh, full of currency.

583
00:29:44,014 --> 00:29:46,381
And one thing that happens is

584
00:29:46,483 --> 00:29:48,716
they all lead
back to the Silk Road.

585
00:29:48,818 --> 00:29:52,687
And you have a number
of independent investigations

586
00:29:52,789 --> 00:29:56,157
sort of cropping up around
the same timeframe

587
00:29:56,259 --> 00:29:57,659
following different leads,

588
00:29:57,761 --> 00:30:00,061
but all leading back
to the same place.

589
00:30:00,163 --> 00:30:01,963
- REEVES NARRATING:
At the same time,

590
00:30:02,065 --> 00:30:04,032
the New York Cyber-Crime
Division of the FBI

591
00:30:04,134 --> 00:30:08,236
began their own investigation,
headed by Agent Chris Tarbell.

592
00:30:08,338 --> 00:30:11,005
- There were people
essentially online 24/7

593
00:30:11,107 --> 00:30:13,675
as part of the team that...
that was monitoring,

594
00:30:13,777 --> 00:30:16,744
gathering, even just the little
bits of evidence.

595
00:30:16,846 --> 00:30:18,813
- REEVES NARRATING:
Informants were activated.

596
00:30:18,915 --> 00:30:20,581
The site was crawling
with law enforcement

597
00:30:20,684 --> 00:30:22,684
posing as vendors and buyers

598
00:30:22,786 --> 00:30:26,020
from the very beginning
of Silk Road's existence.

599
00:30:26,122 --> 00:30:30,892
In early 2012, HSI partnered
with Tarbell's FBI investigators

600
00:30:30,994 --> 00:30:34,228
as well as the DEA to mount
an undercover operation

601
00:30:34,331 --> 00:30:36,597
called "Marco Polo"
with the intention of

602
00:30:36,700 --> 00:30:39,901
penetrating the inner
sanctum of the Silk Road.

603
00:30:40,003 --> 00:30:43,905
- [digitally-altered voice]

604
00:31:16,506 --> 00:31:18,426
- REEVES NARRATING:
The operation gained traction

605
00:31:18,475 --> 00:31:21,876
when an undercover agent using
the vendor name of "nob"

606
00:31:21,978 --> 00:31:24,812
was allegedly able to establish
direct communication

607
00:31:24,914 --> 00:31:26,614
with the Dread Pirate Roberts,

608
00:31:26,716 --> 00:31:29,083
which would lead to
a shocking turn of events.

609
00:31:29,185 --> 00:31:32,320
Nob complained to DPR
about the small-fry nature

610
00:31:32,422 --> 00:31:34,455
of most deals on the Silk Road.

611
00:31:34,557 --> 00:31:36,023
"It really isn't worth it

612
00:31:36,126 --> 00:31:38,793
to do below 10 kilos,"
the agent wrote.

613
00:31:38,895 --> 00:31:41,462
DPR offered to help
find a buyer for nob

614
00:31:41,564 --> 00:31:43,965
and allegedly turned to one
of his most trusted partners

615
00:31:44,067 --> 00:31:47,235
known only as "chronicpain"
to put the deal together.

616
00:31:47,337 --> 00:31:49,871
Chronicpain had been
one of the core administrators

617
00:31:49,973 --> 00:31:51,539
of the Silk Road
from the beginning,

618
00:31:51,641 --> 00:31:53,975
a frequent contributor
to the forums who shared

619
00:31:54,077 --> 00:31:57,745
the Silk Road vision for
reducing harm in the drug trade.

620
00:31:57,847 --> 00:32:00,214
But these halcyon days
were about to end.

621
00:32:00,316 --> 00:32:03,384
In order to facilitate
this drug deal,

622
00:32:03,486 --> 00:32:06,053
chronicpain gave the informant
his home address.

623
00:32:06,156 --> 00:32:08,890
Federal agents immediately
apprehended chronicpain

624
00:32:08,992 --> 00:32:12,260
at his Salt Lake City home
and were surprised to discover

625
00:32:12,362 --> 00:32:16,464
that this 47-year-old family man
named Curtis Clark Green

626
00:32:16,566 --> 00:32:18,566
was a dark net criminal.

627
00:32:18,668 --> 00:32:20,201
- At some point they're going
to catch one of those people.

628
00:32:20,303 --> 00:32:22,136
And what do you do
in a typical drug case?

629
00:32:22,238 --> 00:32:24,772
You roll that person over
as a cooperating witness.

630
00:32:24,874 --> 00:32:27,975
And in this case, one of them
they got really lucky

631
00:32:28,077 --> 00:32:30,178
and he was an administrator
on the system.

632
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:32,180
- REEVES NARRATING:
Green had access to

633
00:32:32,282 --> 00:32:34,749
other Silk Road users' accounts
and financial records,

634
00:32:34,851 --> 00:32:36,751
including Dread Pirate Roberts.

635
00:32:36,853 --> 00:32:38,820
"I have to assume he will sing,"

636
00:32:38,922 --> 00:32:41,522
DPR wrote to nob,
the undercover agent.

637
00:32:41,624 --> 00:32:42,857
"I'd like him beat up."

638
00:32:42,959 --> 00:32:45,159
Then, the next day,
he allegedly wrote,

639
00:32:45,261 --> 00:32:48,863
"Can you change the order to
execute rather than torture?"

640
00:32:48,965 --> 00:32:50,865
A murder was staged.

641
00:32:50,967 --> 00:32:54,001
And a photograph of Green's
bloody body was sent to DPR,

642
00:32:54,103 --> 00:32:56,704
who paid for the hit in Bitcoin.

643
00:32:56,806 --> 00:32:59,407
There would be five more alleged
Murders-For-Hire,

644
00:32:59,509 --> 00:33:03,044
including ordered hits against
a blackmailer, a scammer

645
00:33:03,146 --> 00:33:06,080
and an apparent contract
with the Hells Angels.

646
00:33:06,182 --> 00:33:08,082
The names of two
of these victims

647
00:33:08,184 --> 00:33:09,917
were found to be fictitious.

648
00:33:10,019 --> 00:33:11,085
And authorities have no evidence

649
00:33:11,187 --> 00:33:13,688
of any murders
being carried out.

650
00:33:13,790 --> 00:33:15,857
The alleged attempted
murder of Curtis Green

651
00:33:15,959 --> 00:33:18,459
allowed the authorities
to obtain an indictment

652
00:33:18,561 --> 00:33:19,927
against Dread Pirate Roberts,

653
00:33:20,029 --> 00:33:22,029
charging him with drug offenses,

654
00:33:22,131 --> 00:33:25,032
attempted witness murder
and Murder-For-Hire.

655
00:33:25,134 --> 00:33:27,068
Of course, they still
had no idea

656
00:33:27,170 --> 00:33:29,937
who the Dread Pirate Roberts
actually was.

657
00:33:30,039 --> 00:33:32,974
So the embedded agents continued
to communicate with DPR,

658
00:33:33,076 --> 00:33:35,376
and DPR continued to respond.

659
00:33:36,880 --> 00:33:41,115
In June of 2013,
Ross moved into an apartment

660
00:33:41,217 --> 00:33:43,317
that he found on Craigslist.

661
00:33:43,419 --> 00:33:45,853
Allegedly, he did not give
his roommates his real name

662
00:33:45,955 --> 00:33:48,155
and was known as Joshua Terrey.

663
00:33:48,258 --> 00:33:51,392
At the same time,
IRS agent Gary Alford

664
00:33:51,494 --> 00:33:53,794
was investigating the Silk Road

665
00:33:53,897 --> 00:33:55,596
and through a simple Google
search was able to locate

666
00:33:55,698 --> 00:33:59,133
an early email on the open
internet discussing the launch

667
00:33:59,235 --> 00:34:01,068
of the Silk Road marketplace

668
00:34:01,170 --> 00:34:06,107
and connect that email to an
account owned by Ross Ulbricht.

669
00:34:06,209 --> 00:34:08,042
One month later,
postal inspectors

670
00:34:08,144 --> 00:34:11,379
at the Canadian border
seized a package of fake IDs

671
00:34:11,481 --> 00:34:16,517
with Ross' image that were
en route to his home address.

672
00:34:16,619 --> 00:34:21,389
Ross was visited at his
apartment by several DHS agents.

673
00:34:21,491 --> 00:34:24,492
The agents handed Ross a false
California driver's license

674
00:34:24,594 --> 00:34:27,128
that bore his picture,
but a different name.

675
00:34:27,230 --> 00:34:30,498
Ulbricht denied ownership
or knowledge of the fake IDs,

676
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:34,101
and the agents simply left.

677
00:34:34,203 --> 00:34:37,538
- If you suspect somebody
may be involved in a...

678
00:34:37,640 --> 00:34:39,874
in a large-scale
criminal enterprise,

679
00:34:39,976 --> 00:34:42,143
going and knocking on a door
with some, uh, you know,

680
00:34:42,245 --> 00:34:45,680
some evidence of fake IDs
is important, uh,

681
00:34:45,782 --> 00:34:48,549
because you can see
the guy face-to-face.

682
00:34:48,651 --> 00:34:51,819
Uh, you may get some useful
information out of an interview.

683
00:34:51,921 --> 00:34:54,522
You may or may not want to take
him into custody on the spot.

684
00:34:54,624 --> 00:34:58,059
Let's sit back and let's, uh,
let's really go after this

685
00:34:58,161 --> 00:35:02,029
in a... in a... you know, much
more global way, if you will,

686
00:35:02,131 --> 00:35:05,066
uh, because there's a lot more
here than just one count of,

687
00:35:05,168 --> 00:35:07,501
uh, you know, fake IDs.

688
00:35:07,604 --> 00:35:09,403
- REEVES NARRATING: The next
big break in the case

689
00:35:09,505 --> 00:35:11,539
would be achieved
by FBI agent Tarbell

690
00:35:11,641 --> 00:35:14,542
and his cyber-crime team,
who had somehow located

691
00:35:14,644 --> 00:35:18,112
the Silk Road servers
in Germany and Iceland.

692
00:35:18,214 --> 00:35:19,714
How these hidden
servers were found

693
00:35:19,816 --> 00:35:21,282
has been a matter
of controversy,

694
00:35:21,384 --> 00:35:25,086
but the FBI had their own copy
of the Silk Road server,

695
00:35:25,188 --> 00:35:28,289
and now they hoped to finally
unmask the Dread Pirate Roberts.

696
00:35:42,372 --> 00:35:44,205
- REEVES NARRATING:
Over the course of a year,

697
00:35:44,307 --> 00:35:48,075
a Chicago-based agent from the
DHS named Jared Der-Yeghiayan

698
00:35:48,177 --> 00:35:50,211
had been embedded
in the Silk Road,

699
00:35:50,313 --> 00:35:54,181
now posing as a high-ranking
moderator named "cirrus."

700
00:35:54,283 --> 00:35:56,450
With both the evidence
connecting Ross to the launch of

701
00:35:56,552 --> 00:35:59,387
the Silk Road and the incident
with the fake IDs,

702
00:35:59,489 --> 00:36:03,424
Ross became one of
the primary suspects.

703
00:36:03,526 --> 00:36:05,493
On October 1st in
a coordinated effort

704
00:36:05,595 --> 00:36:10,164
between Der-Yeghiayan from
the DHS and Tarbell's FBI squad,

705
00:36:10,266 --> 00:36:12,299
a sting operation was launched.

706
00:36:12,402 --> 00:36:14,702
According to
Der-Yeghiayan's testimony,

707
00:36:14,804 --> 00:36:17,304
he staked out Ross'
new residence.

708
00:36:17,407 --> 00:36:19,206
And using his
pseudonym of cirrus,

709
00:36:19,308 --> 00:36:21,442
Der-Yeghiayan initiated
a conversation

710
00:36:21,544 --> 00:36:23,611
on the Silk Road with DPR.

711
00:36:23,713 --> 00:36:26,914
Moments later, Ross went
to the Glen Park Library,

712
00:36:27,016 --> 00:36:29,383
apparently to use their Wi-Fi.

713
00:36:29,485 --> 00:36:31,619
And when Der-Yeghiayan
saw that DPR was logged back

714
00:36:31,721 --> 00:36:33,621
into the Silk Road,

715
00:36:33,723 --> 00:36:36,691
he gave the order for Tarbell
and his squad to move in.

716
00:36:36,793 --> 00:36:39,627
- It's an excitement that you
couldn't even buy off Silk Road.

717
00:36:39,729 --> 00:36:42,496
Uh, all the drugs you could buy
on the site, you... you... you...

